# EXPLAIN of the partial-index access paths (spec/design/explain.md §5, indexes.md §9.2/§9.3): a
# full partial-index scan renders `Index scan: using <index>`; a bound over a partial index whose
# predicate the WHERE implies (but does not restate) renders the ordinary `Index bound`. The
# estimates apply the predicate's structural selectivity to the partial index's scan rows
# (estimator.md §7). jed-only output. Format: ../../../design/conformance.md.
# requires: ddl.create_table, ddl.primary_key, ddl.secondary_index, ddl.index_partial, dml.insert, dml.insert_select, dml.delete, query.select, query.where_eq, query.comparison_order, query.order_by, query.limit, query.set_returning, query.explain, dml.explain, query.order_by_index_scan, query.index_partial, query.index_partial_implication, query.index_partial_full_scan, types.i32, types.text, null.three_valued

